:INFO
Art. 27a Demonstration, testing and repairs
Any person wishing to install or operate for demonstration, testing and repair purposes radio equipment that is intended to be operated by authorities to safeguard public security requires authorisation from OFCOM in accordance with Article 59a RFSO.
|

:NOTE
Art. 27a — Inserted by No I of the O of 18 Nov. 2020 (As 2020 6213). Amended by No I of the O of 22 Nov. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 720).
SR 784.102.1
|

:INFO
Art. 28 Restriction on operations
The radio equipment referred to in Article 6 paragraph 2 may only be operated subject to the conditions set out in Articles 53–59a RFSO.
|

:NOTE
Art. 28 — Amended by No I of the O of 22 Nov. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 720).
SR 784.102.1
|

:INFO
Art 28a Correspondence address
Applicants based abroad must provide a correspondence address in Switzerland, in particular for the due service of official communications and rulings.
|

:NOTE
Art. 28a — Inserted by No I of the O of 22 Nov. 2023, in force since 1 Jan. 2024 (AS 2023 720).

:PATH
Section 2 Exhibition and Demonstration
|

:INFO
Art. 29
1 Any person exhibiting radio equipment that does not fulfil the conditions required for making it available on the market must clearly indicate that the equipment is not in conformity with the regulations and that it may not be made available on the market or put into service.
2 Any person who wishes to install and operate for demonstration purposes radio equipment that does not meet the requirements for being made available on the market must obtain the required licence (Art. 30 RFSO).
3 Articles 22 LVEO and 22 OEMC are reserved.
|

:NOTE
Para. 2 — SR 784.102.1
